# TraceOps Dashboard — Frontend UI Description

This document describes the TraceOps dashboard frontend: how it is built, how it fetches
and displays data, and what every page and major component shows in the UI.

Source location: `dashboard/frontend`

---

## 1. Technology stack

A **React 18 + Vite** single-page application (JavaScript, no TypeScript).

| Concern | Library |
|---|---|
| UI framework | React 18.3 |
| Build / dev server | Vite 8 (`npm run dev` on port 5173) |
| Routing | `react-router-dom` v6, routes lazy-loaded via `React.lazy` |
| Server state & caching | `@tanstack/react-query` (15s stale time, optional polling) |
| Data tables | `@tanstack/react-table` |
| Time-series & aggregate charts | `recharts` |
| Topology / node-link graphs | `reactflow` + `dagre` (automatic layout) |
| Markdown rendering (AI reports) | `react-markdown` |
| Date formatting | `date-fns` |
| Icons | `lucide-react` |
| Unit tests | `vitest` + Testing Library |
| E2E / accessibility tests | `playwright` + `@axe-core/playwright` |

Styling is plain CSS split into token/theme/layout/component/explorer/watchdog stylesheets
under `src/styles/`. Theming (dark/light/system) and density (comfortable/compact) are
applied via `data-theme` / `data-density` attributes on `<html>`.

---

## 2. Application shell and architecture

### Entry & auth gate (`App.jsx`)
The app is authentication-gated:
- `AuthContext` bootstraps a session on load.
- While loading → a loading screen.
- If not authenticated → the `Login` page.
- If authenticated → the `ProductShell`.

### ProductShell layout
- **Sidebar** — collapsible, with the TraceOps brand and grouped navigation.
- **Topbar** — mobile menu button, breadcrumbs, global controls, and a user menu.
- **Main area** — the routed page, rendered inside a `Suspense` boundary.
- **Mobile drawer** — slide-out navigation for small screens.

### Navigation groups
| Group | Items (route) |
|---|---|
| **Watchdog** | Overview (`/`), Incidents & RCA (`/incidents`), History (`/incidents/history`) |
| **Investigate** | Graph Maps (`/graphs`) |
| **Explore** | Metrics (`/metrics`), Logs (`/logs`), Traces (`/traces`), Infrastructure (`/infra`) |
| **Analytics** | Statistics (`/stats`) |

Additional routes: incident detail (`/incidents/:reportId`), history detail
(`/incidents/history/:incidentId`), and a legacy `/rca` → `/incidents` redirect.

### Global controls (topbar)
- **Service scope** — free-text service filter.
- **Time-range picker** — relative window (15m/30m/1h/2h/6h/24h) or an absolute from/to range.
- **Auto-refresh** — off / 15s / 30s / 60s.
- **Refresh button** — dispatches a `watchdog:refresh` event and invalidates all React Query caches.

### User menu
Theme toggle (dark/light), density toggle (compact/comfortable), and sign out.

---

## 3. State management

### `DashboardContext`
- Holds **global filters** (service, time window, refresh interval) synchronized to the
  **URL query string**, so views are shareable and bookmarkable.
- Holds **preferences** (theme, density, sidebar collapsed, saved views) persisted to
  `localStorage`.
- Exposes `filters`, `preferences`, `setFilter`, `setPreference`, `resetFilters`, `timeMode`.

### `AuthContext`
- Loads the session, exposes `login()` / `logout()` / `bootstrap()`.
- Listens for the `traceops:unauthorized` event (fired on 401) to drop the session.
- Stores a CSRF token used by the API client.

### API layer (`src/api/`)
- **`client.js`** — `apiFetch` wrapper: JSON body handling, cookie credentials, CSRF header
  injection on mutating requests, and a `traceops:unauthorized` event on 401. Throws a
  typed `ApiError` with status + code.
- **`queries.js`** — shared `QueryClient` (retry except on 401/403, 15s stale time) and the
  `useApiQuery` hook plus `queryKeys` factory.
- **`incidents.js`** (~600 lines) — the heavy **normalization layer**. It defensively
  reshapes messy/legacy backend RCA payloads into stable UI shapes:
  incident history items, RCA report detail, causal hypotheses, five confidence dimensions,
  telemetry-coverage grouping, supporting/contradicting evidence, and LLM enrichment. It
  also builds evidence deep-links (`evidenceLink`) that pivot from an evidence item into the
  correct telemetry explorer (Metrics / Logs / Traces / Topology / change timeline).
- **`useFetch.js`** — a thin React Query wrapper returning `{ data, loading, error, reload }`
  with optional `refreshMs` polling.

Each frontend area maps to a FastAPI backend router: `/api/alerts`, `/api/metrics`,
`/api/logs`, `/api/traces`, `/api/infra`, `/api/graphs`, `/api/incidents`, `/api/rca`,
`/api/stats`.

---

## 4. Pages

### Watchdog group

#### Overview (`/`)
The operational landing page. Shows:
- **Alert banner** — count of active alerts and the top 5 (alert name, service, summary).
- **Health summary** — KPI cards (active alerts, recent incidents, complete analyses,
  needs-investigation, degraded services).
- **Highest-priority insights** — top 6 incidents as `InsightCard`s.
- **Incident activity card** — an incidents-per-day sparkline plus total incidents and
  average confidence KPIs.
- **Service health card** — grid of up to 8 services with health dot, error rate, p99
  latency, RPS, and an error-rate bar.
- **Result summary** — scope/window/refresh badges.

#### Incidents & RCA (`/incidents`) — the incident inbox
- **Search + sort + filter form** — free-text search; sort by highest priority / newest /
  highest confidence; minimum-confidence filter; automation-eligibility filter.
- **Faceted filter sidebar** (`FacetPanel`) — severity, analysis quality, failure type,
  routing, root service, with counts.
- **Table / Cards view toggle** — table (`IncidentTable`) or card grid (`InsightCard`).
- **Saved views** — persist the current query under a name (localStorage).
- **Pagination** — 25 per page, offset-based.
- Priority sorting is applied client-side when the sort is "highest priority".

#### Incident Investigation (`/incidents/:reportId`) — the centerpiece (~1000 lines)
A 7-tab RCA report explorer. Header shows severity/analysis-status/incident-status chips, an
"active alert" chip when correlated, the title, root-cause summary, and a **conservative
aggregate confidence gauge** (explicitly labelled "not a probability"). A **Re-run analysis**
button appears when the report is reanalysis-eligible.

Contextual banners:
- **Calibration-not-fitted warning** when confidence is uncalibrated.
- **Historical report warning** when analysis is older than 24h.
- **Analysis-failure panel** when telemetry backends were unavailable (distinguishes an
  analysis-system failure from an unknown application root cause).
- **Compact warnings** grouping per-service metric-unavailable warnings.

Tabs:
1. **Overview** —
   - **RCA story** (numbered 1–3): Root cause, Critical failure, Impact.
   - **Causal hypotheses** — a side-by-side comparison table of two selectable hypotheses:
     root set, failure type, heuristic score, score decomposition, supporting/refuting
     evidence, causal paths, counterfactual / path coverage, unexplained residuals, and
     evidence strength/basis, with an auto-generated comparison rationale.
   - **Confidence panel** — 5 dimensions with `<meter>` bars (root ranking, failure type,
     causal consistency, evidence coverage, automation safety) plus calibration metadata.
   - **Quality panel** — telemetry outcomes grouped by backend/signal (success/empty/error
     counts, record counts) plus calibration and automation-eligibility.
   - **Impact panel** — observed affected services vs. topology-derived predicted exposure.
   - **Changes panel** — deployment/Kubernetes changes near the incident (observed vs.
     context-only), revisions, resource versions, images.
   - **Investigation scope** and **Anomaly profile** (sparkline of anomaly scores).
   - **Historical analogs** — grid of similar past incidents with similarity %.
   - **Feedback form** — accept/reject verdict; on reject, optional corrected root service,
     corrected failure type, and missing-evidence list; posts to `/api/rca/:id/feedback`.
2. **Evidence** — supporting and contradicting evidence items, each with observed values vs.
   baseline, score, timestamp, reproducibility (window/query/reference/source), and a
   deep-link to its source telemetry explorer.
3. **Timeline** — causal narrative (or legacy events), sortable oldest/newest, with phase
   tags, uncertainty labels, and evidence reference links.
4. **Topology** — three views (incident snapshot / current reconstruction / comparison),
   with provenance notices and, in comparison mode, a diff summary plus two side-by-side
   topology graphs.
5. **Related telemetry** — pivot links into Metrics, Logs, Topology, and each persisted
   trace, carrying the persisted incident window.
6. **AI-generated report** — clearly marked non-authoritative; shows synthesis status
   (complete/fallback/disabled/error/unavailable), provider/model/latency/source-digest
   metadata, a classification review (agrees/disagrees with canonical RCA), the rendered
   Markdown report, and collapsible structured JSON.
7. **Raw** — the raw report JSON.

Keyboard navigation (arrow/Home/End) moves between tabs; the active tab is stored in the URL.

#### History (`/incidents/history`)
A durable incident lifecycle archive:
- **List view** — search, service autocomplete, failure-type filter, date-range presets
  (all/24h/7d/30d), sort, status radio (active/resolved/all), and pagination (25/page).
  Table columns: incident ID, status chip, root service, analysis status, confidence %,
  report-version count, first/last seen.
- **Detail view** (`/incidents/history/:incidentId`) — breadcrumb, header with alert name
  and status chips; a durable definition list (alerted service, root cause, failure type,
  first/last/resolved timestamps); a list of immutable RCA report versions (each linking to
  its investigation); and a chronological lifecycle event timeline.

### Investigate group

#### Graph Maps (`/graphs`)
A multi-layer topology explorer with 4 tabs, all rendered via `TopologyGraph`:
- **Services** — live service dependency map.
- **Infrastructure** — live node/pod/infra map.
- **Trace execution** — a selected trace's span graph (choose from recent traces).
- **Incident subgraph** — a selected RCA report's incident topology.
Each tab has legend chips for node/edge types.

### Explore group (telemetry browsers, built on the shared `Explorer` framework)

#### Metrics (`/metrics`)
Per-service performance comparison using a **Recharts `ComposedChart`**: stacked baseline
area + observed line + anomaly scatter, for error rate (%), p99 latency (ms), and request
rate (req/s). Includes a service sidebar with health dots and stat cards (current, baseline,
delta %, health) plus per-metric anomaly counts and a rolling baseline reference line.

#### Logs (`/logs`)
Loki log viewer: full-text search, level dropdown (error/warn/info/debug), source-label
dropdown, a **24-bucket volume histogram**, a facet sidebar with source counts, and
expandable rows showing JSON detail and a clickable trace-ID link (200-log limit).

#### Traces (`/traces`)
Tempo trace explorer: sidebar of up to 50 recent trace IDs (searchable, "errors only"
toggle); a detail pane with stats (E2E duration, span count, service count, error spans); a
**span waterfall** with hierarchical indentation, critical-path highlighting (amber) and
error spans (red); and a per-span inspector.

#### Infrastructure (`/infra`)
Kubernetes cluster view: side-by-side **Nodes** table (CPU %, memory %, condition badges) and
**Pods** table (namespace, restart count, status), with search and status filter; 5 stat
cards (node/pod counts, average CPU/memory, unhealthy count); and a live `TopologyGraph`
that can focus on a selected node's connected resources.

### Analytics group

#### Statistics (`/stats`)
RCA aggregates rendered with **Recharts**: stat cards (total reports, classification-coverage
%, average confidence, failure-type count); a coverage progress bar; a failure-distribution
**pie chart**; a top-affected-services **bar chart**; and a reports-per-day **bar chart**
(last 30 days).

### Login (`/login` gate)
Centered branded card with username/password inputs, a submitting state, and an error box
(clears the password on failure).

---

## 5. Shared components

### `TopologyGraph.jsx` (ReactFlow + dagre) — the most complex component
- Automatic top-to-bottom **dagre layout**; custom node component; `fitView`, zoom 0.2–2,
  pan, and ReactFlow controls.
- **Node coloring** by status/kind: nodes/infra (grey/yellow/red by condition & CPU), pods
  (green/yellow/red by restart count), spans (red on error), services (blue/green).
- **Edge styling** by type and error rate; edges animate when error rate ≥ 5% or on trace
  calls; labels show request rate or p99 latency.
- **Causal overlay** driven by the primary hypothesis: root-cause nodes (purple outline),
  causal-path nodes/edges (cyan; edge width scales with evidence strength), contradictions
  (dashed orange), unexplained residuals (dotted yellow), with a legend.
- **Inspector panel** — selected node's metadata (type, namespace, condition, restarts, CPU/
  memory %, service, host, operation, duration, status code) and incoming/outgoing degree.
- Selecting a node dims unrelated nodes/edges and thickens connected edges.
- **Accessible text summary** — a `<details>` list of all nodes and connections.

### Watchdog components (`src/components/watchdog/`)
- **HealthSummary** — the 5 KPI cards described under Overview.
- **InsightCard** — compact incident card: severity/analysis-status chips, automation-
  suppressed chip, clickable title, summary, and a meta row (service, failure type,
  confidence %, timestamp); prefetches the incident on hover. Exports `incidentPriority`.
- **IncidentTable** — clickable rows with columns: detected, finding (+ severity chip),
  root service, quality, confidence %, routing.
- **FacetPanel** — grouped filter checkboxes with counts and a clear button.
- **AnomalySparkline** — a small responsive SVG polyline of anomaly scores.

### Explorer framework (`src/components/explorer/Explorer.jsx`)
Shared building blocks for the Explore pages: `ExplorerHeader`, `ExplorerSummary`,
`ExplorerState` (loading/error/empty), `ExplorerField`, `FacetButton`, plus helpers
`formatDuration`, `setUrlParams`, and `initialUrlParam`.

